1
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:24,260
Anyone without money, come to my place.

2
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:28,940
I don't have any either, but don't worry.

3
00:00:28,940 --> 00:00:36,040
Look at the blue sky and white clouds.

4
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:08,000
Nuisance old man, Goshogawara.

5
00:01:12,680 --> 00:01:15,440
Honda, it's nice weather, isn't it?

6
00:01:16,360 --> 00:01:22,380
The two-night, three-day luxury Izu-Hakone trip for two I won in the neighborhood raffle,
Goshō experience.

7
00:01:22,840 --> 00:01:25,520
This must be the result of
my good deeds all these years.

8
00:01:26,260 --> 00:01:30,140
The one who won that was me,
not you, senior.

9
00:01:30,980 --> 00:01:35,340
Besides, I was going to invite Nana-chan,
not you, but you...

10
00:01:35,340 --> 00:01:38,140
Say something to him, Honda.

11
00:01:38,520 --> 00:01:40,240
No, it's nothing.

12
00:01:40,940 --> 00:01:45,000
The train is approaching.
Please wait behind the white line.

13
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,500
Hey, perfect timing, and...

14
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:51,780
What is this?

15
00:01:53,920 --> 00:01:55,700
What a strange train

16
00:01:56,780 --> 00:01:59,260
Just as expected of the
luxurious Izu-Hakone trip!

17
00:02:00,140 --> 00:02:00,340
Again!

18
00:02:01,440 --> 00:02:02,500
W-what's going on?

19
00:02:03,240 --> 00:02:04,500
You can't ride this train!

20
00:02:04,720 --> 00:02:06,180
Hey, what do you think you're doing!

21
00:02:06,700 --> 00:02:09,680
This is a private train!
Regular people aren't allowed on!

22
00:02:09,940 --> 00:02:11,140
A private train, you say?

23
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:13,020
I've composed a haiku!

24
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:17,280
W-what?

25
00:02:21,900 --> 00:02:23,840
Cosmos slipping down the slope,

26
00:02:23,890 --> 00:02:26,080
a train journey in the dappled sunlight!

27
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:28,440
Chugga-chugga, chugga-chugga,
chugga-chugga-chugga-chugga!

28
00:02:30,140 --> 00:02:33,540
Chugging along together,
chug, chug, chug, chug!

29
00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:36,420
What's with that old guy?

30
00:02:36,420 --> 00:02:38,320
How rude!

31
00:02:38,320 --> 00:02:41,120
Listen, the one over there is

32
00:02:41,120 --> 00:02:42,900
the president of the Goshogawara Group.

33
00:02:42,900 --> 00:02:44,920
Goshogawara Kingoro-no-suke.

34
00:02:44,920 --> 00:02:47,060
He is none other than Sazaemon Tarō-sama!

35
00:02:47,060 --> 00:02:48,100
Masaki

36
00:02:48,860 --> 00:02:50,560
I'm terribly sorry, President.

37
00:02:50,560 --> 00:02:52,620
Some ordinary passengers mistakenly

38
00:02:52,620 --> 00:02:55,640
tried to board the
president's private train, so

39
00:02:56,160 --> 00:02:57,220
I came up with one!

40
00:02:57,740 --> 00:02:58,100
Hello.

41
00:02:58,100 --> 00:03:02,020
Hello! I'm President Goshogawara!

42
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:06,160
Well done! As expected of the president!

43
00:03:06,460 --> 00:03:08,920
Splendid! I'm deeply moved!

44
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:10,020
Looks like a challenge

45
00:03:10,740 --> 00:03:13,280
Odawara, your train is over there, right!

46
00:03:18,540 --> 00:03:20,720
What on earth are those guys?

47
00:03:21,240 --> 00:03:23,720
If I remember right, the Goshogawara Group

48
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:26,600
makes everything from
playing cards to space rockets.

49
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:29,460
It's one of the biggest
corporations in Japan.

50
00:03:30,080 --> 00:03:33,240
I heard the president there is
a total one-man show, though.

51
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:35,220
So that's him

52
00:03:36,060 --> 00:03:38,720
I see, a one-man president
and his subordinates.

53
00:03:38,720 --> 00:03:41,640
Unemployment's high these days, too.

54
00:03:41,640 --> 00:03:44,840
Everyone's desperate not to get fired.

55
00:03:44,840 --> 00:03:49,220
I forgot something really important!

56
00:03:50,720 --> 00:03:51,520
W-what is it?

57
00:03:51,660 --> 00:03:52,420
Ekiben!

58
00:03:53,680 --> 00:03:56,040
Let's see, bento shop, bento shop...

59
00:03:56,040 --> 00:03:57,440
Over there!

60
00:03:58,240 --> 00:03:58,960
No way.

61
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:01,200
Yes, what is it, President?

62
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:02,780
I've come up with a haiku!

63
00:04:03,160 --> 00:04:06,060
When your stomach growls, it's time to eat.

64
00:04:06,060 --> 00:04:09,720
Ben-ben-ben, I just love bento so much!

65
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:13,480
Ekiben! Bring the President some ekiben!

66
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:20,040
President,
that was truly a magnificent haiku!

67
00:04:21,280 --> 00:04:23,120
Which one should I pick?

68
00:04:23,360 --> 00:04:23,660
Heh heh.

69
00:04:25,580 --> 00:04:26,700
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

70
00:04:26,780 --> 00:04:27,160
Aitoku!

71
00:04:27,220 --> 00:04:27,700
Here you go!

72
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:29,680
I got here first, damn it!

73
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:32,240
I'll pay for it!

74
00:04:32,500 --> 00:04:33,280
Give me all of them!

75
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:34,200
Thank you for your business!

76
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:35,320
What?!

77
00:04:35,320 --> 00:05:03,860


78
00:05:09,500 --> 00:05:10,800
Ward One is done!

79
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:14,800
Ring-ring-ring,
the bell rings, the bell mark!

80
00:05:15,300 --> 00:05:17,560
So many bento boxes, how fun!

81
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:18,840
Well done!

82
00:05:21,180 --> 00:05:23,880
Hey, don't take them all!

83
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:29,360
Just one, come on, go on!

84
00:05:43,160 --> 00:05:45,980
Wow, what a great view!

85
00:05:46,700 --> 00:05:54,860
Senpai, you should look too, it feels great!
I missed my breakfast and I'm starving. Looking at scenery won't fill your stomach.

86
00:05:55,280 --> 00:05:55,520
No way.

87
00:06:04,240 --> 00:06:07,000
Eating this just makes me hungrier.

88
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:08,520
Haven't had dinner yet, have we?

89
00:06:09,100 --> 00:06:10,420
It's still daytime, you know.

90
00:06:12,980 --> 00:06:14,800
There's a tennis court too.

91
00:06:15,460 --> 00:06:16,860
It's all girls!

92
00:06:16,860 --> 00:06:18,340
Could they be college students?

93
00:06:19,440 --> 00:06:21,500
There's a cute one over there, isn't there!

94
00:06:23,840 --> 00:06:24,240
Yes.

95
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:24,440
Yes!

96
00:06:31,220 --> 00:06:34,600
Look at them go, going at it.
Being young is nice, isn't it.

97
00:06:35,480 --> 00:06:38,180
Senpai, weren't you starving?

98
00:06:38,560 --> 00:06:41,882
Dinner will come out on time,
even if we leave it be.

99
00:06:41,932 --> 00:06:43,860
Right now it's about romance, not food.

100
00:06:50,640 --> 00:06:52,420
Is the person in charge here?

101
00:06:52,760 --> 00:06:53,160
Yes.

102
00:06:54,400 --> 00:06:55,800
May I help you with something?

103
00:06:58,080 --> 00:07:00,420
We're reserving this entire
car for the Goshogawara Group.

104
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:02,200
Make sure no other passengers get in.

105
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:04,000
Yes.

106
00:07:10,860 --> 00:07:12,240
That's so infuriating.

107
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:12,940
Worst.

108
00:07:13,820 --> 00:07:15,520
Those people from earlier...

109
00:07:15,520 --> 00:07:17,880
So those guys were here too?

110
00:07:20,160 --> 00:07:22,300
The president is ready.

111
00:07:29,360 --> 00:07:30,080
How about it?

112
00:07:30,080 --> 00:07:32,460
It suits you very well, President.

113
00:07:34,480 --> 00:07:36,300
What kind of getup is he wearing?

114
00:07:36,300 --> 00:07:39,020
He doesn't look like he plays tennis at all,
does he?

115
00:07:40,020 --> 00:07:41,320
I've got a haiku.

116
00:07:41,320 --> 00:07:42,700
Tennis is...

117
00:07:42,700 --> 00:07:45,780
Is it a "mistake" in your hand, or a
"male" in your hand?

118
00:07:45,780 --> 00:07:48,840
Ace, ace, ace, ace, aim for the ace!

119
00:07:50,160 --> 00:07:51,920
What a splendid haiku, President.

120
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:58,900
Hey, let's go back to the room
and take a bath or something.

121
00:07:58,900 --> 00:07:59,980
Yeah, sounds good.

122
00:08:00,960 --> 00:08:02,560
Another haiku.

123
00:08:02,560 --> 00:08:06,040
Tennis, where even the women sway,

124
00:08:06,040 --> 00:08:09,500
If you're going to do it anyway,
teach me too, topknot and all!

125
00:08:09,500 --> 00:08:12,360
W-wonderful!

126
00:08:12,980 --> 00:08:15,900
No, that's not what the president meant.

127
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:20,560
Is there no female coach here?

128
00:08:21,920 --> 00:08:23,760
No, I'm the only coach here.

129
00:08:23,760 --> 00:08:25,020
Damn it!

130
00:08:25,860 --> 00:08:28,300
Find a female coach right away!

131
00:08:28,520 --> 00:08:29,020
Hurry!

132
00:08:29,400 --> 00:08:29,660
Yes!

133
00:08:31,180 --> 00:08:32,120
Female coach?

134
00:08:32,300 --> 00:08:38,620
Female coach!

135
00:08:41,160 --> 00:08:42,440
W-what are those guys?

136
00:08:42,600 --> 00:08:44,100
They're making a huge fuss.

137
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:45,800
It's got nothing to do with us.

138
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:47,020
Hey! You there!

139
00:08:47,740 --> 00:08:50,480
Does anyone know a female tennis coach?

140
00:08:52,060 --> 00:08:54,240
Bring one here right away
as soon as you find her.

141
00:08:54,240 --> 00:08:56,200
You can't just suddenly ask
us for something like that.

142
00:08:56,200 --> 00:08:58,800
I'll pay whatever it takes, I beg you.

143
00:08:58,800 --> 00:09:02,460
So any female coach will do, right?
Any kind at all?

144
00:09:03,280 --> 00:09:04,720
Do you know someone?

145
00:09:04,720 --> 00:09:06,360
Leave it to me.

146
00:09:06,760 --> 00:09:07,960
Sorry to keep you waiting.

147
00:09:13,520 --> 00:09:13,960
That's right.

148
00:09:15,920 --> 00:09:17,480
Hey, what do you think you're doing?

149
00:09:17,480 --> 00:09:19,460
How about it? It suits me, doesn't it?

150
00:09:19,460 --> 00:09:21,740
How is that a female coach?

151
00:09:21,740 --> 00:09:23,540
He just took a run-up, that's all!

152
00:09:23,540 --> 00:09:26,360
In short, as long as I look like a female coach,
that's enough, right?

153
00:09:26,360 --> 00:09:27,940
This is good enough.

154
00:09:27,940 --> 00:09:28,660
Senpai

155
00:09:28,660 --> 00:09:29,680
No way, no way.

156
00:09:29,680 --> 00:09:30,780
I see.

157
00:09:30,780 --> 00:09:31,980
No way...

158
00:09:31,980 --> 00:09:32,740
Yes.

159
00:09:32,740 --> 00:09:34,500
The wig's ready!

160
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:35,820
Wonderful!

161
00:09:35,820 --> 00:09:38,200
To the arrival of the female coach...

162
00:09:38,200 --> 00:09:40,340
My arms have turned to lead.

163
00:09:40,340 --> 00:09:42,540
Hurry up, let's do it together!

164
00:09:44,900 --> 00:09:47,560
See? It's fine, isn't it?

165
00:09:47,560 --> 00:09:50,780
I never knew this was the
type of woman you liked.

166
00:09:50,780 --> 00:09:52,420
I didn't know either.

167
00:09:53,920 --> 00:09:54,800
Nice to meet you.

168
00:10:01,640 --> 00:10:04,360
What's wrong? Please hit it back.

169
00:10:05,720 --> 00:10:08,120
Aim for the president's racket.

170
00:10:08,120 --> 00:10:10,680
What is that?
At this rate, it won't be tennis at all!

171
00:10:11,240 --> 00:10:14,840
If you let the president run around like that and he gets injured,
what do you plan to do?

172
00:10:14,840 --> 00:10:17,520
Then don't go wanting to play
tennis in the first place!

173
00:10:17,520 --> 00:10:20,140
If you want the money, do exactly as I say.

174
00:10:21,640 --> 00:10:22,580
Fine, I get it.

175
00:10:23,920 --> 00:10:24,560
Here I go.

176
00:10:25,640 --> 00:10:26,620
Take that one!

177
00:10:30,220 --> 00:10:31,520
Take that one!

178
00:10:44,640 --> 00:10:46,380
Yes, it hit!

179
00:10:50,020 --> 00:10:52,720
Aw, too bad, it's out.

180
00:10:53,340 --> 00:10:55,140
What a brilliant shot, Mr. President!

181
00:10:55,140 --> 00:10:57,840
It's better than a pro's!
Nobody can return that.

182
00:10:58,380 --> 00:11:01,700
When it comes to tennis,
I'm unbeatable by anyone.

183
00:11:02,700 --> 00:11:04,560
What? That one was out!

184
00:11:06,160 --> 00:11:09,180
The president's shot can't possibly be out,
you know.

185
00:11:09,700 --> 00:11:11,340
Don't you want the money?

186
00:11:11,340 --> 00:11:12,640
Fine, fine.

187
00:11:12,640 --> 00:11:14,100
I got it, I'm in!

188
00:11:14,680 --> 00:11:18,080
In the tennis I watched on TV some time ago,

189
00:11:18,080 --> 00:11:21,620
the ball kept going back and forth,
back and forth, back and forth,

190
00:11:21,620 --> 00:11:25,300
back and forth,
back and forth, back and forth.

191
00:11:25,300 --> 00:11:27,120
The president wants a rally!

192
00:11:27,840 --> 00:11:28,840
A rally?

193
00:11:29,380 --> 00:11:30,680
No, I get it!

194
00:11:31,340 --> 00:11:33,700
Can they even have a rally with that?

195
00:11:34,120 --> 00:11:36,290
Guess I've got no choice but to do it.

196
00:11:36,340 --> 00:11:38,560
Here I come! Let's go!

197
00:11:41,820 --> 00:11:47,480
Keep the rally going!

198
00:11:47,820 --> 00:11:51,320
Don't be unreasonable! You lot just sit back and watch,
taking it easy!

199
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:53,460
Are you alright, senpai?

200
00:11:54,480 --> 00:11:56,180
I've got a great idea!

201
00:11:58,520 --> 00:12:00,540
With this, we can have a rally!

202
00:12:00,540 --> 00:12:03,240
I see, so that was an option.

203
00:12:03,240 --> 00:12:04,820
Here I come!

204
00:12:04,820 --> 00:12:08,560
Now's the time to win!

205
00:12:12,560 --> 00:12:13,600
Girl

206
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:15,300
Girl

207
00:12:15,300 --> 00:12:18,280
Girl

208
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:18,820
Tea

209
00:12:18,820 --> 00:12:20,280
Cake

210
00:12:20,280 --> 00:12:21,120
Dadada

211
00:12:21,120 --> 00:12:22,000
Tea

212
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:22,900
Cake

213
00:12:22,900 --> 00:12:24,540
Dadada

214
00:12:24,540 --> 00:12:25,380
Tea

215
00:12:25,880 --> 00:12:26,360
Cake

216
00:12:26,360 --> 00:12:28,800
Is this really tennis?

217
00:12:38,020 --> 00:12:39,620
I've composed a haiku!

218
00:12:40,160 --> 00:12:42,580
Tennis is so much fun,

219
00:12:42,580 --> 00:12:45,060
I'd love to play together again.

220
00:12:45,060 --> 00:12:45,840
Here we go!

221
00:12:47,360 --> 00:12:48,580
Congratulations.

222
00:12:48,580 --> 00:12:51,480
I'll never do this again!

223
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:53,500
Such an idiotic tennis match.

224
00:13:09,560 --> 00:13:11,280
You really eat a lot, don't you?

225
00:13:11,280 --> 00:13:14,120
I did get some exercise yesterday,
after all.

226
00:13:14,120 --> 00:13:15,580
That must have been tough

227
00:13:16,100 --> 00:13:18,280
But you got paid a lot, didn't you?

228
00:13:19,420 --> 00:13:21,320
Let's have a blast today.

229
00:13:23,120 --> 00:13:25,900
These guys are up so
early in the morning, too.

230
00:13:27,540 --> 00:13:27,940
Hey.

231
00:13:30,040 --> 00:13:31,460
Thanks for yesterday.

232
00:13:31,460 --> 00:13:32,940
Going somewhere?

233
00:13:32,940 --> 00:13:36,840
The president suddenly said
he wants to play golf, so...

234
00:13:38,740 --> 00:13:40,740
Should I tag along too?

235
00:13:40,740 --> 00:13:42,980
Knowing that guy,

236
00:13:42,980 --> 00:13:46,280
he's going to make some outrageous demand,
just like yesterday, isn't he?

237
00:13:47,540 --> 00:13:49,800
That's quite possible, but

238
00:13:49,800 --> 00:13:52,300
if it's me, I can handle it.

239
00:13:54,640 --> 00:13:56,460
Got it, please do.

240
00:13:56,460 --> 00:13:59,700
In return, you'd better pay
up generously on the puns too.

241
00:14:00,520 --> 00:14:01,500
Leave it to me.

242
00:14:04,460 --> 00:14:06,480
I'm going out with the Goshogawara guy.

243
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:08,960
Then what am I supposed to do?

244
00:14:08,960 --> 00:14:10,400
Just go off and play on your own.

245
00:14:11,680 --> 00:14:12,080
No way...

246
00:14:18,960 --> 00:14:20,700
Did he reserve the whole place again?

247
00:14:20,700 --> 00:14:21,800
Of course.

248
00:14:21,800 --> 00:14:23,440
I've got a haiku!

249
00:14:23,440 --> 00:14:24,820
In one shot.

250
00:14:24,820 --> 00:14:26,320
I'll sink it, you'll see.

251
00:14:26,320 --> 00:14:27,100
Hototogisu.

252
00:14:27,100 --> 00:14:28,040
Hoo-hoo.

253
00:14:28,040 --> 00:14:28,660
Hole... in the end.

254
00:14:28,660 --> 00:14:29,820
That's a bush warbler.

255
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:33,520
The president's going for a hole-in-one!

256
00:14:33,520 --> 00:14:34,040
What?

257
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:35,880
Cover for me, will you?

258
00:14:40,960 --> 00:14:42,080
Here you go.

259
00:14:48,060 --> 00:14:50,000
Goshogawara

260
00:14:54,480 --> 00:14:55,920
What did you do?

261
00:14:55,920 --> 00:14:59,440
This is bad.

262
00:15:01,360 --> 00:15:03,240
Leave it to me.

263
00:15:06,880 --> 00:15:07,560
Ugh!

264
00:15:07,640 --> 00:15:08,280
Whoa!

265
00:15:12,740 --> 00:15:14,780
Oh no! It's going out!

266
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:15,260
Ugh!

267
00:15:15,640 --> 00:15:16,900
Hehe-hehe!

268
00:15:17,160 --> 00:15:17,800
Urk!

269
00:15:17,960 --> 00:15:18,640
Urk!

270
00:15:18,640 --> 00:15:19,280
It's hot!

271
00:15:25,540 --> 00:15:28,420
Chief! Splendid! That's a hole-in-one!

272
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:34,160
Riding a horse,
I'd love to gallop on and on!

273
00:15:34,300 --> 00:15:35,580
La-la-la!

274
00:15:36,880 --> 00:15:39,280
A horse!
The chief wants to go horseback riding!

275
00:15:39,620 --> 00:15:42,680
What? He just started golf,
for crying out loud!

276
00:15:50,920 --> 00:15:53,020
Why do we have to be horses?

277
00:15:53,400 --> 00:15:56,960
Because real horses won't listen
to what the president says!

278
00:15:57,640 --> 00:15:59,737
Autumn, dusk, the mountains turn red.

279
00:15:59,787 --> 00:16:02,580
It's a maple-leaf hunt, everyone assemble!

280
00:16:02,800 --> 00:16:03,760
A maple-leaf hunt!

281
00:16:08,060 --> 00:16:09,760
Isn't that a little off?

282
00:16:09,760 --> 00:16:11,600
As long as the president is satisfied.

283
00:16:12,480 --> 00:16:16,180
When it comes to Izu,
it's obviously The Izu Dancer.

284
00:16:16,180 --> 00:16:17,360
It's The Izu Dancer!

285
00:16:18,540 --> 00:16:22,160
Next year, this month,
tonight, this very moon.

286
00:16:23,460 --> 00:16:25,860
Uh-oh, this is The Golden Demon!

287
00:16:25,860 --> 00:16:27,960
If we keep quiet, no one will notice.

288
00:16:29,920 --> 00:16:33,560
The sea is wide,
the sea is big, all I do is fish.

289
00:16:33,560 --> 00:16:35,140
Hana-chan, I envy you!

290
00:16:38,960 --> 00:16:42,420
Speaking of fishing,
I really want to catch a sea bream.

291
00:16:42,420 --> 00:16:45,320
If you're from Kyushu,
you'd want to catch tai, wouldn't you?

292
00:16:45,320 --> 00:16:47,240
The president is hoping for tai!

293
00:16:47,240 --> 00:16:49,980
But how do we get him to catch one?

294
00:16:49,980 --> 00:16:51,460
Leave it to me.

295
00:16:51,460 --> 00:16:53,960
Come on in, come on in!

296
00:16:54,480 --> 00:16:55,600
Cheap, cheap!

297
00:16:57,140 --> 00:16:57,780
Hey, old man!

298
00:16:57,780 --> 00:16:59,660
Welcome! What'll it be?

299
00:17:00,120 --> 00:17:00,820
All of it.

300
00:17:01,560 --> 00:17:02,600
What did you say, you bastard?

301
00:17:03,060 --> 00:17:03,460
Here, this should do.

302
00:17:04,900 --> 00:17:06,080
Thanks for your business!

303
00:17:06,880 --> 00:17:08,400
Was it tai?

304
00:17:08,860 --> 00:17:12,120
Leave the rest to you!
I'll stay by the president's side.

305
00:17:15,780 --> 00:17:17,120
Yes, got it!

306
00:17:24,760 --> 00:17:26,480
Boss, it's a bite!

307
00:17:29,500 --> 00:17:32,320
Boss, it's a tai! Congratulations!

308
00:17:32,780 --> 00:17:35,800
Bazaar! Bazaar! Bazaar!

309
00:17:36,880 --> 00:17:39,580
And I'm a fishing genius,
if I do say so myself!

310
00:17:40,180 --> 00:17:40,560
Splendid!

311
00:17:44,400 --> 00:17:45,500
Next up, octopus!

312
00:17:45,660 --> 00:17:48,200
Chu-chu-chu, octopus-kai-na!

313
00:17:48,320 --> 00:17:48,980
Next up, octopus!

314
00:17:49,040 --> 00:17:50,200
It's octopus, you know!

315
00:17:50,660 --> 00:17:51,880
How about octopus?

316
00:17:52,240 --> 00:17:55,700
Well, I bought up the whole shop,
so we've got everything!

317
00:17:55,700 --> 00:17:57,380
Sh-sh-sh, here you go!

318
00:18:02,500 --> 00:18:03,880
Boss, here it comes!

319
00:18:03,880 --> 00:18:04,200
Well then

320
00:18:04,200 --> 00:18:06,900
Ahhhhhh

321
00:18:06,900 --> 00:18:08,220
Ahhhhhh

322
00:18:14,560 --> 00:18:23,840
Maybe I'll try catching a suzuki too. Next up is suzuki,
suzuki! Oh no, we're out of suzuki!

323
00:18:26,860 --> 00:18:27,920
Excuse me.

324
00:18:29,560 --> 00:18:30,320
What's wrong?

325
00:18:30,320 --> 00:18:32,880
Goshogawara, do you know a lot about fish?

326
00:18:32,880 --> 00:18:35,480
No, not at all.

327
00:18:35,480 --> 00:18:36,320
Got it.

328
00:18:38,600 --> 00:18:39,820
That's good enough, right?

329
00:18:45,540 --> 00:18:47,420
Splendid work, Mr. President.

330
00:18:47,420 --> 00:18:49,360
Banzai! Banzai!

331
00:18:51,060 --> 00:18:54,160
The wind's getting cold already.

332
00:18:54,160 --> 00:18:55,020
I think I'll head home.

333
00:18:55,020 --> 00:18:57,820
Right, then let's arrange a car right away.

334
00:18:58,620 --> 00:19:05,100
Before we go home, I'd like to land one big catch.
What should it be? Orca sounds good.

335
00:19:05,100 --> 00:19:10,620
Orca, orca, orca, orca, orca, orca.
It's gotta be orca!

336
00:19:10,620 --> 00:19:15,160
We haven't even made any
preparations for everyone.

337
00:19:15,160 --> 00:19:22,760
Of course. Did you really think amateurs like us could catch anything?
I told you we don't know much about fish.

338
00:19:22,760 --> 00:19:24,860
What happens if we don't catch anything?

339
00:19:25,580 --> 00:19:27,700
We'll all be laid off.

340
00:19:27,700 --> 00:19:31,780
In this era of severe job shortages,
we'll be left out on the streets.

341
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:35,100
Then what about my reward?

342
00:19:35,200 --> 00:19:36,460
How could we possibly pay that?

343
00:19:36,460 --> 00:19:37,000
What?

344
00:19:38,160 --> 00:19:42,560
I have three daughters,
the eldest in her third year of junior high!

345
00:19:44,160 --> 00:19:45,820
Who on earth is calling at a time like this?

346
00:19:45,820 --> 00:19:46,780
Hello?

347
00:19:46,780 --> 00:19:48,620
It's me, senior.

348
00:19:48,620 --> 00:19:50,560
What do you want, Honda?

349
00:19:51,120 --> 00:19:54,380
I'm at an aquarium called
Ode Marine Park right now.

350
00:19:54,380 --> 00:19:56,520
They're putting on an amazing show.

351
00:19:56,520 --> 00:19:57,400
Guess what it is?

352
00:19:57,920 --> 00:19:59,200
I don't care what it is.

353
00:20:02,740 --> 00:20:04,460
It's an orca, an orca!

354
00:20:04,460 --> 00:20:07,180
They're putting on an amazing orca show!

355
00:20:07,900 --> 00:20:08,740
Orca?

356
00:20:09,340 --> 00:20:11,280
Where is it? Tell me right now.

357
00:20:13,180 --> 00:20:13,900
What did you say?

358
00:20:14,120 --> 00:20:15,840
You said they'd lend us an orca?

359
00:20:16,160 --> 00:20:17,780
Don't talk nonsense.

360
00:20:18,840 --> 00:20:20,320
Here's the rental fee.

361
00:20:21,620 --> 00:20:23,760
Please, let me take it along.

362
00:20:24,660 --> 00:20:26,720
But how are we going to transport it?

363
00:20:28,080 --> 00:20:30,080
That's what you're here for, isn't it?

364
00:20:30,080 --> 00:20:31,460
This is it.

365
00:20:35,040 --> 00:20:35,880
Get in, Honda!

366
00:20:36,500 --> 00:20:37,220
Yes, yes.

367
00:20:37,220 --> 00:20:38,100
Let's start with him.

368
00:20:42,140 --> 00:20:43,720
Hey, Mister Consul, hurry up and get on!

369
00:20:43,720 --> 00:20:44,600
Hurry!

370
00:20:44,980 --> 00:20:45,940
Open the floodgate!

371
00:20:47,780 --> 00:20:52,920
Eeeeeh, is it ready yet?
Is it ready yet? Is the photo ready yet?

372
00:20:53,490 --> 00:21:00,980
Hey, what are we supposed to do in a situation like this?
I have no idea. Without Masaki-san, I'm totally lost on how to react.

373
00:21:00,980 --> 00:21:05,800
President, Saku-san,
President, look at that!

374
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:06,420
Me

375
00:21:09,420 --> 00:21:11,500
Honda! Keep the bus going straight ahead!

376
00:21:11,800 --> 00:21:14,220
It's Ryo's, but thank you so much!

377
00:21:14,600 --> 00:21:16,800
It's an orca! The orca has arrived!

378
00:21:23,700 --> 00:21:25,500
What's going on, Honda!

379
00:21:26,600 --> 00:21:28,492
No,

380
00:21:28,542 --> 00:21:31,780
I don't know!

381
00:21:31,980 --> 00:21:35,700
Maybe because it's a show orca,
it feels like there's a show going on!

382
00:21:35,960 --> 00:21:36,280
Whoa!

383
00:21:36,280 --> 00:21:41,000
It's fun, it's fun, orcas really are big!

384
00:21:52,240 --> 00:21:53,620
It's coming this way!

385
00:21:55,920 --> 00:21:57,980
It's dangerous! Let's evacuate!

386
00:21:57,980 --> 00:22:03,340
Wait! We're about to catch an orca,
sell it, and be overjoyed!

387
00:22:03,340 --> 00:22:04,120
President!

388
00:22:07,320 --> 00:22:09,140
President!

389
00:22:09,140 --> 00:22:12,060
President!

390
00:22:12,060 --> 00:22:18,200
President!

391
00:22:18,200 --> 00:22:25,700
President!

392
00:22:25,700 --> 00:22:28,280
President!

393
00:22:29,240 --> 00:22:31,280
It's over.

394
00:22:31,500 --> 00:22:33,580
Everything's already...

395
00:22:37,180 --> 00:22:38,100
Hey, are you all right?

396
00:22:40,180 --> 00:22:41,220
Masaki.

397
00:22:41,220 --> 00:22:41,700
Yes.

398
00:22:41,700 --> 00:22:43,200
I just came up with a haiku.

399
00:22:43,200 --> 00:22:45,540
Sayonara, sayonara, sayonara.

400
00:22:46,120 --> 00:22:48,140
Well then, everyone, sayonara.

401
00:22:49,860 --> 00:22:51,360
Looks like you're fired after all.

402
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:53,580
Hold on, Goshogawara!

403
00:22:55,060 --> 00:22:59,580
These guys have desperately put
up with your selfishness until now.

404
00:22:59,960 --> 00:23:03,140
And you're going to fire
them over one single mistake?

405
00:23:03,580 --> 00:23:05,820
Is that really what the president
of a major company should do?

406
00:23:08,080 --> 00:23:08,840
Hey.

407
00:23:08,840 --> 00:23:11,180
This train car we got from
yesterday's tennis match.

408
00:23:11,180 --> 00:23:12,620
We don't need this junk.

409
00:23:12,620 --> 00:23:14,580
Cancel their dismissals.

410
00:23:16,860 --> 00:23:20,180
I have no intention of firing you at all.

411
00:23:20,700 --> 00:23:22,980
It's cold,
so we're just going back to the hotel.

412
00:23:24,780 --> 00:23:25,540
President

413
00:23:25,540 --> 00:23:26,900
Since we're here,

414
00:23:26,900 --> 00:23:29,140
We'll be getting our money back.

415
00:23:30,180 --> 00:23:31,980
And they all lived happily ever after.

416
00:23:31,980 --> 00:23:32,860
Hooray, everything turned out great!

417
00:23:33,580 --> 00:23:34,220
Wa-wa-wa-wait a minute!

418
00:23:34,220 --> 00:23:38,020
Thanks for your hard work, everyone.
Tonight we're having a party!

419
00:23:38,020 --> 00:23:40,940
Banzai, banzai, banzai!

420
00:23:40,940 --> 00:23:41,700
Thank you very much.

421
00:23:46,800 --> 00:23:49,060
W-why did it turn out like this?

422
00:23:49,580 --> 00:23:51,760
Then give back the money, you idiot.

423
00:23:55,800 --> 00:23:58,020
Anyway, it's like this...

424
00:23:58,020 --> 00:24:01,720
Why did you only save me?

425
00:24:14,200 --> 00:24:20,180
The rain that's just stopped,
as if someone is calling out.

426
00:24:46,400 --> 00:24:49,820
Thank you for watching.

427
00:24:50,180 --> 00:24:53,360
We were kids back then,
but everyone's forgotten.

428
00:24:54,500 --> 00:24:57,540
Politicians with their self-important faces,

429
00:24:57,970 --> 00:25:00,800
and the aunties who
are a thorn in your side,

430
00:25:00,800 --> 00:25:06,440
turn around that corner, won't you?

431
00:25:07,480 --> 00:25:11,620
You can meet everyone, everyone!

432
00:25:13,700 --> 00:25:16,240
Over there is Kameari.

433
00:25:17,640 --> 00:25:19,360
Yes, surely it's Kameari.

434
00:25:19,360 --> 00:25:24,860
Everyone, come on over to our town!

435
00:25:25,920 --> 00:25:26,320
Thank you.

436
00:25:29,040 --> 00:25:34,940
Even though you're a rookie violinist who's sure to
win the 10 million yen prize at the Vienna competition,

437
00:25:34,940 --> 00:25:37,460
you lost your wallet and
can't make it to Narita?

438
00:25:37,600 --> 00:25:39,520
Alright, leave it to me.

439
00:25:39,520 --> 00:25:43,520
Anyone who won't bet on a dead-sure thing like this is a total fool,
I'm telling you.

440
00:25:43,520 --> 00:25:45,780
Next time: Fooled in Kameari!

441
00:25:46,240 --> 00:25:48,020
And see you in Narita, okay?

